            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>GPDMA_C11LLR</name>
          <displayName>GPDMA_C11LLR</displayName>
          <description>GPDMA channel 11 linked-list address register </description>
		  <alternateRegister>GPDMA_C9LLR</alternateRegister>
          <addressOffset>0x54C</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>LA</name>
              <description>If UT1 = UT2 = UB1 = USA = UDA = ULL = 0 and if LA[15:20] = 0, the current LLI is the last one. The channel transfer is completed without any update of the linked-list GPDMA register file.
Else, this field is the pointer to the memory address offset from which the next linked-list data structure is automatically fetched from, once the data transfer is completed, in order to conditionally update the linked-list GPDMA internal register file (GPDMA_C11TR1, GPDMA_C11TR2, GPDMA_C11BR1, GPDMA_CxSAR, GPDMA_CxDAR and GPDMA_C11LLR).
Note: The user must program the pointer to be 32-bit aligned. The two low-significant bits are write ignored. </description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>14</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ULL</name>
              <description>This bit is used to control the update of GPDMA_C11LLR from the memory during the link transfer.
0: no GPDMA_C11LLR update
1: GPDMA_C11LLR update
</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>no GPDMA_C11LLR update</description>
                  <value>0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>GPDMA_C11LLR update</description>
                  <value>1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>UB2</name>
              <description>This bit controls the update of GPDMA_CxBR2 from the memory during the link transfer.
0: no GPDMA_CxBR2 update
1: GPDMA_CxBR2 update
</description>
