                  <description>When KEYVALID is set and KEYSEL[2:0]=0 application can transfer the ownership of the SAES, with its loaded key, to an application running in another security context (such as nonsecure, secure).</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>When KEYVALID is set, key error flag (KEIF) is set when an access to any registers is detected, this access having a security context (for example, secure, nonsecure) that does not match the one of the application that loaded the key.</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
